  "description": "\"Dynamic loop state does not cross the procedure boundary any more than a variable does\" (spec/execution-model.md:673-680): `repcount` reports the turn of the `repeat` that LEXICALLY encloses it, and `h`'s body encloses none, so calling it from inside a live `repeat` body raises `ol-repcount-outside-repeat` (spec/error-model.md:120) rather than reporting the caller's turn. Measured: a runtime that lets a call inherit the caller's turn stack prints `1` and then `2` here, with no diagnostic, and passes every other `repcount` fixture in the corpus. The existing `repcount-in-a-handler-has-no-enclosing-repeat` pins the deferred-handler shape; this is the procedure-boundary shape, which is a different sentence of the same section.",
